🔴 13. Docker Swarm
# What is Docker Swarm?

Docker Swarm Docker ka native container orchestration tool hai jo multiple Docker hosts ko ek cluster ki tarah manage karta hai.

Jab containers ki sankhya badh jati hai aur unhe manually manage karna mushkil ho jata hai, tab Docker Swarm use kiya jata hai.

> Why Docker Swarm is Used?
Multiple containers manage karne ke liye
High availability provide karne ke liye
Load balancing ke liye
Container scaling ke liye
Cluster management ke liye
# Swarm Cluster

Swarm Cluster multiple Docker machines (nodes) ka group hota hai jo ek single system ki tarah kaam karta hai.

Cluster me manager aur worker nodes hote hain.

> Why Swarm Cluster is Used?
Large-scale applications run karne ke liye
Fault tolerance provide karne ke liye
Workload distribute karne ke liye
Centralized management ke liye
# Manager Node

Manager Node Swarm Cluster ka master node hota hai jo cluster ko control aur manage karta hai.

Ye scheduling aur orchestration decisions leta hai.

Responsibilities:
Cluster manage karna
Worker nodes monitor karna
Services deploy karna
Scaling decisions lena
Why Manager Node is Used?
Cluster control ke liye
Resource allocation ke liye
Service management ke liye
Worker Node

Worker Node wo node hota hai jo actual containers run karta hai.

Manager se instructions receive karke tasks execute karta hai.

Responsibilities:
Containers run karna
Assigned tasks execute karna
Resource provide karna
Why Worker Node is Used?
Application workload handle karne ke liye
Containers execute karne ke liye
Cluster resources provide karne ke liye
Services in Swarm

Service Docker Swarm me application deployment unit hoti hai.

Service define karti hai ki kitne containers (replicas) run honge aur kaunsi image use hogi.

Why Services are Used?
Application deployment ke liye
Container replicas manage karne ke liye
Desired state maintain karne ke liye
High availability ke liye

Example:
Agar service me 3 replicas define hain aur 1 container fail ho jaye, to Swarm automatically naya container create kar dega.

Scaling Containers

Scaling ka matlab containers ki sankhya badhana ya kam karna hai according to workload.

Why Scaling is Used?
High traffic handle karne ke liye
Better performance ke liye
High availability ke liye
Resource optimization ke liye
Example:

Traffic badhne par 2 containers ko 10 containers me scale kiya ja sakta hai.

🔴 14. Docker Security
Security Best Practices

Docker Security Best Practices wo guidelines hain jo containers aur images ko secure banane me help karti hain.

Why Security Best Practices are Important?
Cyber attacks prevent karne ke liye
Unauthorized access rokne ke liye
Sensitive data protect karne ke liye
Secure production environment maintain karne ke liye
Common Practices:
Trusted images use karo
Latest updates apply karo
Unused containers remove karo
Secrets ko code me store mat karo
Minimum permissions do
Image Scanning

Image Scanning ka matlab Docker Images ko vulnerabilities aur security issues ke liye check karna hai.

Why Image Scanning is Used?
Vulnerabilities identify karne ke liye
Insecure packages detect karne ke liye
Compliance maintain karne ke liye
Secure deployments ke liye
Example:

Image me outdated software ya vulnerable library detect karna.

Secure Containers

Secure Containers ka matlab containers ko is tarah configure karna ki security risks minimum ho jaye.

Why Secure Containers are Important?
Container breakout attacks prevent karne ke liye
Data protection ke liye
Secure application execution ke liye
Production security improve karne ke liye
Practices:
Non-root user use karo
Minimal base image use karo
Unnecessary ports expose mat karo
Resource limits define karo
# Secrets Management

Secrets Management sensitive information ko securely store aur access karne ka process hai.

> Examples of Secrets:
Passwords
API Keys
Database Credentials
Access Tokens
> Why Secrets Management is Used?
Sensitive data protect karne ke liye
Hardcoding avoid karne ke liye
Secure deployments ke liye
Compliance requirements fulfill karne ke liye
# Least Privilege

Least Privilege Principle ka matlab hai user, process ya container ko sirf utni hi permissions dena jitni uske kaam ke liye zaroori ho.

Why Least Privilege is Important?
Security risks kam karne ke liye
Unauthorized access rokne ke liye
Attack impact reduce karne ke liye
System security improve karne ke liye
Example:

Agar application ko sirf read access chahiye, to write access nahi deni chahiye.

# Interview Purpose (English)

Q: What is Docker Swarm?
A: Docker Swarm is Docker’s native orchestration tool used to manage and scale containers across multiple hosts.

Q: What is the role of a Manager Node in Docker Swarm?
A: A Manager Node controls the cluster, schedules tasks, and manages services.

Q: What is a Worker Node?
A: A Worker Node executes tasks and runs containers assigned by the Manager Node.

Q: What is Container Scaling?
A: Scaling is the process of increasing or decreasing the number of container replicas based on workload.

Q: Why is Docker Security important?
A: Docker Security protects containers, images, and sensitive data from vulnerabilities and unauthorized access.

Q: What is Image Scanning?
A: Image Scanning is the process of checking Docker images for security vulnerabilities and misconfigurations.

Q: What is the Principle of Least Privilege?
A: It means giving only the minimum permissions required to perform a task, reducing security risks.